  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Formations, &#xe9;tudes et expertises - PFEE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Le projet Formation, &#xe9;tudes et expertises / T&#xe0;ggat, vise &#xe0; renforcer les comp&#xe9;tences du personnel des parties prenantes du portefeuille, notamment, les acteurs en charge de la mise en &#x153;uvre de ses volets op&#xe9;rationnels, les groupes cibles et les entit&#xe9;s publiques et parapubliques qui participent &#xe0; l&#x2019;action. L&#x2019;accent est mis de mani&#xe8;re particuli&#xe8;re sur le d&#xe9;veloppement des comp&#xe9;tences num&#xe9;riques et en management : ceci afin de permettre aux parties prenantes du Portefeuille de s&#x2019;approprier des outils digitaux que les interventions mettront en place et d&#x2019;assurer une gestion efficace des ressources.  Par le financement d&#x2019;une s&#xe9;rie d&#x2019;&#xe9;tudes, l&#x2019;intervention vise aussi &#xe0; la cr&#xe9;ation d&#x2019;une base de connaissances partag&#xe9;es entre le S&#xe9;n&#xe9;gal et la Belgique, qui puissent &#xea;tre utilis&#xe9;e pour am&#xe9;liorer l&#x2019;impact du Portefeuille par l&#x2019;affinement des approches m&#xe9;thodologiques, ou pour d&#xe9;velopper des nouvelles propositions d&#x2019;interventions &#xe0; soumettre &#xe0; des bailleurs tiers.  Les formations, &#xe9;tudes et expertises r&#xe9;alis&#xe9;es dans le cadre de cette intervention 4, devront avoir une valeur compl&#xe9;mentaire et additionnelle par rapport aux appuis pr&#xe9;vus dans les autres interventions 1, 2 et 3 du Portefeuille The Formations, etudes et expertises. PFEE project is a capacity development initiative based in Senegal, falling under the sector unspecified (99810). This project is part of the Belgian-Senegalese Cooperation Programme for the period 2019-2023, which was constructed on the basis of an analysis of convergence points between Senegal&apos;s priorities and those of Belgium&apos;s development cooperation. The &apos;Plan Senegal Emergent Phase II&apos; (PSE II 2019-2023) and various sectoral strategic plans, the national policy for territorial management and development, sectoral policy letters, among others, formed the foundation for discussions. The new directions set by the Belgian Minister of Cooperation, particularly in terms of supporting entrepreneurial agriculture, stimulating private sector growth as a driver of development, promoting a rights-based approach. especially sexual and reproductive health rights. guided the strategic priorities of the new Belgian-Senegalese Cooperation Programme for the 2019-2023 period. Digitalization and new technologies, as well as stimulating innovation in the &apos;green&apos; economy sector, were incorporated into the program, along with synergistic involvement of Belgian cooperation actors, including the private sector and public Belgian institutions (peer2peer). The Law of 2013 on Belgian Development Cooperation recognizes that sustainable development ensures a just transition to sustainable methods of production and consumption, promotes gender equality, and guarantees access to essential public goods and services for the population, as well as respect for their rights, including sexual rights and access to information and services related to sexual and reproductive health. Each man and woman should also have access to productive work under conditions of freedom, equity, safety, and dignity, which implies, among other things, equal opportunities and treatment for all women and men in the workplace. The Decent Work Agenda, as defined by the International Labour Organization (ILO), aims for four strategic objectives, with gender equality being a transversal objective (Article ).</narrative>
  </description>
